    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Leading**: Any tile can be led. 2. **Matching**: Subsequent tiles must match the pips of an open end. 3. **Doubles**: Placed crosswise. They count as the sum of their pips until matched on both sides. 4. **The Spinner**: The first double played is the 'Spinner'. Once matched on its sides, tiles can be played off its ends, creating 4 open ends. 5. **Scoring**: After playing a tile, sum all open ends. If the total is a multiple of 5 (5, 10, 15, 20, etc.), the player immediately scores that many points. 6. **Boneyard**: If you cannot play, you must draw from the boneyard until you can. 7. **Dominoing**: The hand ends when a player uses their last tile. They score the remaining pips in their opponents' hands (rounded to the nearest 5).",
    Player: "1. **Leading**: Any tile can be led. 2. **Matching**: Subsequent tiles must match the pips of an open end. 3. **Doubles**: Placed crosswise. They count as the sum of their pips until matched on both sides. 4. **The Spinner**: The first double played is the 'Spinner'. Once matched on its sides, tiles can be played off its ends, creating 4 open ends. 5. **Scoring**: After playing a tile, sum all open ends. If the total is a multiple of 5 (5, 10, 15, 20, etc.), the player immediately scores that many points. 6. **Boneyard**: If you cannot play, you must draw from the boneyard until you can. 7. **Dominoing**: The hand ends when a player uses their last tile. They score the remaining pips in their opponents' hands (rounded to the nearest 5).",
    objective: 'Be the first to reach the target score (usually 100, 200, or 250) by creating end-totals that are multiples of five.',
    gameplay: "1. **Leading**: Any tile can be led. 2. **Matching**: Subsequent tiles must match the pips of an open end. 3. **Doubles**: Placed crosswise. They count as the sum of their pips until matched on both sides. 4. **The Spinner**: The first double played is the 'Spinner'. Once matched on its sides, tiles can be played off its ends, creating 4 open ends. 5. **Scoring**: After playing a tile, sum all open ends. If the total is a multiple of 5 (5, 10, 15, 20, etc.), the player immediately scores that many points. 6. **Boneyard**: If you cannot play, you must draw from the boneyard until you can. 7. **Dominoing**: The hand ends when a player uses their last tile. They score the remaining pips in their opponents' hands (rounded to the nearest 5).",
    keyRules: [
      'Must play if able. You cannot draw from the boneyard if you have a legal play.',
      "Only the first double is a spinner. All other doubles are 'dead' once matched.",
      "Muggins: If a player fails to claim a scoring total, an opponent may shout 'Muggins!' and take the points for themselves.",
      'If the game is blocked (no one can play), the player with the lowest pip total wins the hand bonus.',
    ],
